REPRODUCER (scratch/s516a/tmpf.pl):
    use IO::File; use Fcntl qw(SEEK_SET SEEK_END);
    my $fh = IO::File->new_tmpfile or die; binmode $fh; print {$fh} "hello";
    seek($fh, 0, SEEK_SET) or die; my $l = <$fh>; print "[$l]\n";
    seek($fh, 0, SEEK_END); print tell($fh), "\n";      # perl: [hello] 5   PCL: [hello] then an unhandled simple-type-error
Backtrace: (FILE-LENGTH #<FD-STREAM for "/tmp/...">) from %p-seek-impl -- SBCL's file-length refuses that fd-stream ('not a stream associated with a file'; the temp file is unlinked or the stream was made from an fd).  SEEK_SET works; SEEK_END needs the size: take it from fstat on the fd (sb-posix:fstat) when file-length refuses.  Also a raw Lisp error escaping a builtin (should be perl-shaped).

